WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.036
Paradev the parallel

00:00:01.848 --> 00:00:03.121
coding-agent desktop

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:04.324
app formerly called

00:00:04.135 --> 00:00:05.750
Superset returns

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:07.685
Paradev reverted its

00:00:07.496 --> 00:00:09.053
February license change

00:00:09.088 --> 00:00:09.984
and is fully

00:00:09.796 --> 00:00:10.892
open source under

00:00:10.704 --> 00:00:11.694
MIT again

00:00:11.907 --> 00:00:13.097
the macOS app

00:00:12.992 --> 00:00:14.135
runs Claude Code

00:00:14.206 --> 00:00:15.503
Codex and other

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:16.435
CLI agents in

00:00:16.246 --> 00:00:17.024
parallel

00:00:17.542 --> 00:00:18.414
The team said

00:00:18.226 --> 00:00:19.263
the more restrictive

00:00:19.075 --> 00:00:20.065
license was a

00:00:19.877 --> 00:00:21.233
mistake and invited

00:00:21.044 --> 00:00:22.023
people to fork

00:00:21.834 --> 00:00:22.695
it or build

00:00:22.507 --> 00:00:23.497
their own product

00:00:23.309 --> 00:00:23.874
on it

00:00:24.398 --> 00:00:26.155
Paradev bundles terminals

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:27.298
code review and

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:28.419
browser previews in

00:00:28.231 --> 00:00:29.586
one workspace and

00:00:29.516 --> 00:00:30.990
isolates each task

00:00:30.813 --> 00:00:31.508
on its own

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.747
branch and worktree

00:00:32.959 --> 00:00:34.138
its GitHub repo

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:34.869
has more than

00:00:34.681 --> 00:00:36.367
16,000 stars

00:00:36.894 --> 00:00:37.908
Full story on

00:00:37.719 --> 00:00:38.615
the dashboard
